The repository is a SageMath-based Python package for Picard-lattice calculations and cylinder-based flexibility searches on del Pezzo surfaces. It has no existing README or command-line entry point; I’m documenting the library APIs, SageMath-based test workflow, and the construction options actually implemented in the source.
Created `README.md` with an overview, SageMath setup and test commands, API guide, construction names and degree constraints, examples, and references. I did not run the tests; no files other than `README.md` were created or edited.

